From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wellken Chen <wellken.chen@cvitek.com.tw>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 10:08:26 +0000
Subject: drivers: soc: sophgo: add CV181x/SG200x TPU driver

Port of the Cvitek TPU character-device driver from the vendor
duo-buildroot-sdk-v2 (Linux 5.10) to mainline. The uAPI is kept
binary-compatible with the vendor SDK so the Cvitek TPU runtime
(libcviruntime) works with minimal changes.

Differences from the vendor driver:
- Android ION replaced with the standard dma-buf importer API; buffers
  come from the CMA dma-buf heap (the TPU has no IOMMU and needs
  physically contiguous memory).
- New GET_DMABUF_PADDR/RELEASE_DMABUF ioctls so userspace can learn a
  buffer's bus address, which vendor ION exposed but mainline heaps do
  not.
- Cache maintenance uses dma_sync_sgtable_*() on the driver's own
  mapping instead of vendor-patched arch symbol exports.
- TEE paths dropped (stubs on cv181x in the vendor tree), 5.10 compat
  ifdefs collapsed, error-path bugs in open()/submit() fixed.

- Hardening beyond the vendor driver: the command-buffer header and
  the descriptor tables it points at are bounds-checked against the
  dma-buf (and the header is consumed from a kernel snapshot), PIO
  copies must lie inside a dma-buf the caller registered, the
  completion interrupt is gated on an executing job instead of open
  file handles, and profiling-timer teardown cannot race the handler
  re-arming it.

Signed-off-by: Wellken Chen <wellken.chen@cvitek.com.tw>
